# Flat top-level node_modules of real directories, not symlinks. The Astro
# Netlify adapter traces the SSR output's dependencies and copies them into the
# function bundle; with a symlinked top level (shamefully-hoist) that trace
# silently misses packages, verified here by the SSR dependency gate reporting
# six missing after switching. A real-directory layout copies completely.
#
# v20 used shamefully-hoist plus [functions.ssr] external_node_modules because
# its adapter did not trace dependencies at all. @astrojs/netlify 6.6.0 does, so
# that pairing is no longer the right shape for this repo.
#
# The cost: one flat top level means a root development tool can shadow a package
# the applications run on. `githits` pulled express, express pinned cookie 0.7,
# and Astro 7's prerenderer — which needs cookie 2 — resolved to the 0.7 copy and
# failed the build. Keep CLI tooling out of the workspace root; there is no pnpm
# setting that says which version wins the top level.
node-linker=hoisted
